1
00:03:27,692 --> 00:03:33,692
Prepare for awesomeness.

2
00:06:55,384 --> 00:07:01,384
Kung Fu Panda is a animation, family, comedy film directed by Mark Osborne.

3
00:10:23,076 --> 00:10:29,076
Chosen by prophecy but doubted by all, Po is an unlikely Dragon Warrior—a clumsy panda thrust
into the world of kung fu as a deadly enemy threatens the Valley of Peace.

4
00:13:50,769 --> 00:13:56,769
Guided by Master Shifu and the Furious Five, Po must embrace who he
is to unlock the power that no scroll can teach.

5
00:17:18,461 --> 00:17:24,461
Po (voice), played by Jack Black.

6
00:20:46,153 --> 00:20:52,153
Tigress (voice), played by Angelina Jolie.

7
00:24:13,846 --> 00:24:19,846
Shifu (voice), played by Dustin Hoffman.

8
00:27:41,538 --> 00:27:47,538
Tai Lung (voice), played by Ian McShane.

9
00:31:09,230 --> 00:31:15,230
Monkey (voice), played by Jackie Chan.

10
00:34:36,923 --> 00:34:42,923
Viper (voice), played by Lucy Liu.

11
00:38:04,615 --> 00:38:10,615
Kung Fu Panda is a 2008 American animated martial arts comedy film directed by John Stevenson and Mark Osborne
and written by Jonathan Aibel and Glenn Berger from a story by Ethan Reiff and Cyrus Voris.

12
00:41:32,307 --> 00:41:38,307
Produced by DreamWorks Animation, it is the first
installment in the Kung Fu Panda franchise.

13
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Starring Jack Black as the voice of the titular character, the film, set in a version of ancient China populated by
anthropomorphic animals, centers on a bumbling giant panda named Po, a kung fu enthusiast living in the Valley of Peace.

14
00:48:27,692 --> 00:48:33,692
When the savage snow leopard Tai Lung is foretold to escape imprisonment and attack the Valley, Po is unwittingly named the "Dragon
Warrior", a prophesied hero worthy of reading a scroll that has been intended to grant its reader limitless power.

15
00:51:55,384 --> 00:52:01,384
The film began development in October 2004, and was initially
conceived as a parody of martial arts films.

16
00:55:23,076 --> 00:55:29,076
However, director Stevenson decided instead to make an action-comedy wuxia film that
incorporated the hero's journey narrative for the lead character.

17
00:58:50,769 --> 00:58:56,769
The project was announced in September 2005.

18
01:02:18,461 --> 01:02:24,461
As with most DreamWorks Animation films, the score for Kung Fu Panda was composed
by Hans Zimmer, on this occasion collaborating with John Powell.

19
01:05:46,153 --> 01:05:52,153
Zimmer visited China to absorb the culture, and used the China
National Symphony Orchestra as part of the scoring process.

20
01:09:13,846 --> 01:09:19,846
Kung Fu Panda premiered at the 2008 Cannes Film Festival on May 15, 2008, and was
theatrically released in the United States on June 6 by Paramount Pictures.

21
01:12:41,538 --> 01:12:47,538
It grossed $632 million on a budget of $130 million, making it the third highest
grossing film of 2008 and the highest-grossing animated film of the year.

22
01:16:09,230 --> 01:16:15,230
It received positive reviews from critics, and was nominated for Best Animated
Feature at the Academy Awards, and the Golden Globe Awards.

23
01:19:36,923 --> 01:19:42,923
The film's success spawned a franchise including three sequels;
the first, Kung Fu Panda 2, was released in 2011.

24
01:23:04,615 --> 01:23:10,615
The film explores themes of martial arts, kung fu, strong woman, china, tiger.

25
01:26:32,307 --> 01:26:38,307
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
